-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",238,{
[7585]="700248A5\n1\tDefeat bats in the Rockbelly Pit (total: 5)\tBats can be found in the Rockbelly Pit cave, which can be entered in the courtyard near the Berghold or from the overlooking Winterheight. You should defeat bats in the Rockbelly Pit to ensure that the Shrine to Skorgrím remains clean.\n2\tVisit the Shrine to Skorgrím in the Rockbelly Pit\tThe Shrine to Skorgrím is in the Rockbelly Pit. You should visit the shrine to see what all the fuss over Skorgrím is about.\n3\tTalk to Gormr Doursmith at the Berghold\tGormr awaits you at the Berghold in Thorin's Gate. You should return to Gormr after having completed the task he gave you.\n",
[7586]="7002292A\n1\tTalk to Cal Sprigley to assess the Blackwold threat in the south\tCal Sprigley can be found at his farm in the southernmost part of Archet. You should speak with Cal Sprigley to assess the reality of the Blackwold threat.\n",
[7587]="7003612C\n1\tUse the bedroll in the Hunter's Lodge to get some rest\tA hunter has offered you a bedroll in the Hunter's Lodge you can use to rest.\n2\tTell the hunter about your curious dream\tYou had a most curious dream, and should share it with the hunter in the Hunter's Lodge.\n",
[7588]="700361C9\n1\tUse the bedroll to get some rest\tA miner has offered you a bedroll you can use to rest.\n2\tTell the miner about your curious dream\tYou had a most curious dream, and should share it with the miner who recommended you rest.\n",
[7589]="70000E1E\n1\tTalk to Dwalin\tDwalin asked you to travel with him to Skorgrím's tomb and put an end to the Dourhands' mad schemes. You should speak with him again when you are ready to leave.\n2\tTalk to Dwalin\tDwalin asked you to travel with him to Skorgrím's tomb and put an end to the Dourhands' mad schemes. You should speak with him again when you are ready to leave.\n3\tTalk to Skógi\030Talk to Eilian\t[see journal]\n",
[7590]="7002280E\n1\tSee for yourself how Amdir fares\tAmdir, very pale and wounded, is sitting in Archet near The Mad Badger Inn. You should check on Amdir, for he was stabbed last night while helping to rescue you and the two hobbits from the Blackwolds.\n2\tLearn why Strider is torn\tStrider kneels beside his friend Amdir, near The Mad Badger Inn in the village of Archet. You should speak with Strider, for Amdir implied that Strider's need is the more pressing.\n",
[7591]="70000031\n1\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tJon Brackenbrook can be found at the Hunter's Lodge that lies along the road east of Archet. Captain Brackenbrook, uncertain of whom to trust, has asked you to speak with his son Jon and earn his aid. He promised to reward you handsomely if you succeed.\n",
[7592]="70022A8D\n1\tBrackenbrook is hopeless -- you should ask Strider what to do\tStrider has not yet left Archet, but he is anxious to leave so that he can pursue his true charge. Strider is a wise Ranger who has seen many evil things come to pass; you should ask him what to do.\n2\tAsk the exiled hunter to come to Archet's aid\tJon Brackenbrook, the exiled son of the Captain, can be found in the Hunter's Lodge to the north-east of Archet. You should appeal to Jon Brackenbrook and his hunters to come to the aid of the besieged town.\n",
[7593]="7002481D\n1\tExplore the gate at the Silver Deep Mine's courtyard\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n2\tFollow the trail of red flowers down the road\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine and grow along the road. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n3\tFollow the trail of red flowers down the road\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine and grow along the road. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n4\tFollow the trail of red flowers down the road\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine and grow along the road. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n5\tFollow the trail of red flowers down the road\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine and grow along the road. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n6\tFollow the trail of red flowers down the road\tThe \"Blood-red footsteps\" begin at the Silver Deep Mine and grow along the road. Elladan suspects that they lead to wherever Skorgrím now lies. You should follow the red flowers to their end, examining each for signs, for they grow where Skorgrím's corpse corrupted the land as he was moved over it.\n7\tTalk to the longbeard dwarf spying nearby\tAn unfriendly-looking keep now stands before you. You should scout the keep, for the trail indicates that Skorgrím's body may have been moved here.\n",
[7594]="70001059\n1\tSearch dead goblins (total: 4)\tThe corpses of the slain goblins lie to the east of Elladan, surrounding the pool there. Elladan killed several goblins and wants you to search the dead for clues, while he remains at his post.\n2\tBring the dwarf pick-axes to Elladan\tElladan awaits you to the west of the pool. Your search revealed that many of the goblins carried dwarf-made pick-axes. Elladan will be most interested in your find.\n",
[7595]="70022923\n1\tQuestion Otto the Brigand about his ties to the Blackwolds\tOtto the Brigand is being held in the stocks in the Archet Jailyard, across the lane from Strider and Amdir. You should question Otto directly about Calder Cob and the Blackwolds' treachery; Captain Brackenbrook is not ready to be convinced by your words alone.\n2\tTalk to the jailor about Otto's foreboding words\tThe Archet jailor, a man named Ned Pruner, stands warily near Otto. You should speak with Ned Pruner, for perhaps Otto had a loose tongue around his captor.\n3\tTalk to Captain Brackenbrook\tCaptain Brackenbrook is in the town of Archet. You should quickly tell Captain Brackenbrook about what Otto has said to you and to Ned Pruner, his jailor.\n",
[7596]="70001068\n1\tDeliver the dwarf pick-axes to Dwalin at Frerin's Court\030Collect dwarf pick-axes (total: 10)\tDwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, west of the Silver Deep. Boggarts line the way out of Edhelion. Elladan has instructed you to take the dwarf-made picks to Dwalin and tell him of the goblins in the Silver Deep. He also suggested you slay some boggarts and learn if they, too, carry the picks.\n",
[7597]="700248BF\n1\tCollect black stones for the Ritual of Commemoration (total: 4)\tThe ritual stones can be found in and around the Rockbelly Pit, east of the Berghold at Thorin's Gate. You should collect black stones for the commemorative ritual being prepared by the Dourhands.\n2\tBring the ritual stones to Bjarni\tBjarni is at the Berghold in the southern area of Thorin's Gate. You should speak with Bjarni and give him the black stones you have collected.\n",
[7598]="7000015D\n1\tDefeat a Blackwold spy and search him\tBlackwold spies may be found to the south-east of the sheep-farm, between the farm and Bronwe's Folly. Dirk Mudbrick wants to discover what the Blackwold spies have learned. He has asked you to confront one of the spies and recover any orders or messages he might be carrying.\n2\tTalk to Dirk Mudbrick\030Collect Sprigley's Note\tDirk Mudbrick can be found at the sheep-farm south and west of Archet. Dirk Mudbrick will be anxious to read the orders you found on the Blackwold spy. You should bring them to him as quickly as possible.\n3\tTalk to Captain Brackenbrook\030Collect Sprigley's Note\tCaptain Brackenbrook can be found inside The Mad Badger Inn, north of the Archet gate. Dirk Mudbrick sent you to Captain Brackenbrook with the orders you found on the Blackwold Spies.\n",
[7599]="7000002F\n1\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunting Lodge, east of Archet. Jon Brackenbrook is waiting for you to join his company.\n2\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunting Lodge, east of Archet. Jon Brackenbrook is waiting for you to join his company.\n3\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\030Talk to Mundo Sackville-Baggins\t[see journal]\n",
[7600]="70018F4D\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Savage Strikes\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Savage Strikes. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Champion Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Champions rely on Fervour to activate some of their skills such as Savage Strikes. Use your Swift Strike and Wild Attack skills to build 2 Fervour and then strike the Targeting Dummy with your Savage Strikes skill.\n2\tSpeak with the Champion Trainer\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7601]="70019396\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Savage Strikes\tYou should talk to the trainer again and learn the skill Savage Strikes. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Champion Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it, then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Champions rely on Fervour to activate some of their skills such as Savage Strikes. Use your Swift Strike and Wild Attack skills to build 2 Fervour and then strike the Targeting Dummy with your Savage Strikes skill.\n2\tTalk to the Champion Trainer at Frerin's Court\tThe Champion Trainer is in Frerin's Court. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7602]="700194A3\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Savage Strikes\tUse yourSavage Strikes on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Champions rely on Fervour to activate some of their skills such as Savage Strikes. Use your Swift Strike and Blade Wall skills to build 3 Fervour and then strike the Targeting Dummy with your Savage Strikes skill.\n2\tTalk to the Champion Trainer in Archet\tThe Champion Trainer is at Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your new skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7603]="700586BD\n1\tUse your Overhand Smash skill on the Training Dummy (total: 3)\tUse your new skill Overhand Smash on the training dummy nearby. Brawlers rely on Mettle to activate some of their skills such as Overhand Smash. Use your Low Strikeor Dextrous Hook to build 3 Mettle and then strike the Training Dummy with your Overhand Smash skill.\n2\tTalk to Otto Beecher, the Brawler Trainer in Archet\tOtto Beecher, the Brawler Trainer, is in Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your new skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7604]="700228A9\n1\tDefeat wolves around Bronwe's Folly (total: 4)\030Search atop Bronwe's Folly for the source of the wolves\tWolves can be found near Archet, and seem to be most concentrated around Bronwe's Folly. Calder Cob, a trusted soldier of Captain Brackenbrook, has asked you to look into Archet's wolf problem.\n2\tUse the Blackwold Banner to summon the offender (Do not leave the platform)\tYou found a strange banner atop the ruins at Bronwe's Folly. You should take a closer look at this banner....\n3\tAsk Calder Cob why he set you up to be ambushed\tCalder Cob stands at the farm just down the road from Archet. Before you go back to Strider, you should ask him why he tried to have you ambushed by Blackwolds.\n",
[7605]="70019508\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Defensive Strike\tUse Defensive Strike on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as Quick Thrust and Shield-bash to build more powerful Gambit attacks. To use your Defensive Strike skill, attack a Training-Dummy with your Shield-bash ability twice. This should cause your Gambit Default skill to change into your Defensive Strike skill. Use your Defensive Strike ability to strike a Training-Dummy.\n2\tTalk to the Warden Trainer in Archet\tThe Warden Trainer is in Archet, in the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used Defensive Strike, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7606]="700248D6\n1\tTalk to Dwalin in Frerin's Court\tDwalin stands by his sick dwarves in Frerin's Court, below the Mirkstone Tunnels. You should bring Elrohir's remedy to Dwalin and tell him of the dire warnings of the fell spirit you encountered in the cave.\n2\tAdminister Elrohir's draught to Bogi\tThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank. You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.\n3\tAdminister Elrohir's draught to Selur\tThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank. You should administer Elrohir's draughte to the sick dwarves.\n4\tAdminister Elrohir's draught to Olin\tThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank. You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.\n5\tAdminister Elrohir's draught to Mathi Stouthand\tThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank. You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.\n6\tTell Dwalin that there is now hope for the dwarves of his party\tDwalin is in Frerin's Court at Thorin's Gate. You should speak with Dwalin about how to proceed now that his dwarves have received a remedy.\n",
[7607]="700244E8\n1\tTalk to Dorniel about her memories of Edhelion\tThe ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands. You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.\n2\tTalk to Naithriel about her memories of Edhelion\tThe ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands. You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.\n3\tTalk to Dorongur about his memory of Skorgrím's death\tThe ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands. You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.\n",
[7608]="70024793\n1\tDefeat pests as you seek Skorgrím's body (total: 4)\tThe Silver Deep Mine is west of the ruins of Edhelion, at the bottom of the stair-path leading down the Mountain. You should follow the stairs down and enter the Silver Deep Mine to search for Skorgrím's body once again.\n2\tFind the site where Skorgrím's body was found\tThe place where Skorgrím's body was discovered deep in the mine, where the sun touches the old ruined cellars of Edhelion. You should seek Skorgrím's body once more to ensure that it does not walk as it did in Elrond's dream.\n3\tCollect one of the strange, red flowers\tYou have found the site of Skorgrím's body, but...the body is nowhere to be found. Instead, red flowers are in its place. You should pick up one of the fell red flowers to bring to Elladan.\n4\tBring the odious red flower to Elladan\tElladan awaits your return at the Edhelion Watch. You should return to Elladan with the flower you collected from the site of Skorgrím's grave.\n",
[7609]="7002591F\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Cook to learn more about cooking and set yourself on a path to good eating.\t\n2\tThe Novice Cook provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the hard biscuit recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a cup of spring barley flour\tThe Novice Cook provided you with the ingredients necessary to create hard biscuits. First, however, you must prepare one of the most important ingredients: a cup of spring barley flour.\n4\tUsing the ingredients you have obtained, cook a hard biscuit\tThe cup of spring barley flour is complete, and you are now ready to make the hard biscuit, as instructed by the Novice Cook.\n5\tThe recipe is complete. Do not eat or sell the hard biscuit! It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Cook.\t\n",
[7610]="700626AC\n1\tSpeak with the Novice Cook in Lhan Garan to learn more about cooking.\t\n2\tThe Novice Cook provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the hard biscuit recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a cup of spring barley flour through the crafting panel\tThe Novice Cook provided you with the ingredients necessary to create hard biscuits. First, however, you must prepare one of the most important ingredients: a cup of spring barley flour. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the cooking tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: in order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Cooking typically requires an oven or camp-fire.\n4\tUsing the ingredients you have obtained, cook a hard biscuit at an oven\tThe cup of spring barley flour is complete, and you are now ready to make the hard biscuit, as instructed by the Novice Cook. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the cooking tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: in order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Cooking typically requires an oven or camp-fire.\n5\tThe recipe is complete. Do not eat or sell the hard biscuit! It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Cook.\t\n",
[7611]="7006278F\n1\tTalk to Undeg\t\n2\tChoose a vocation with the Mistress of Apprentices in order to unlock Introductory crafting quests. Complete three introductory crafting quests.\t\n",
[7612]="70025AF1\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Farmhand to learn more about farming and set yourself on a path to good eating.\t\n2\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to grow the yellow onion. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Farmers are normally purchased from vendors or discovered while farming. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, plant a yellow onion field\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a yellow onion. First, however, you must plant your yellow onion field.\n4\tCollect the fair yellow onion crop\030Activate the Track Crops skill\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a yellow onion. You must now harvest your yellow onion field and obtain a fair yellow onion crop. To find the field, activate the Track Crops skill.\n5\tUsing the ingredients you have, pick a yellow onion at the workbench\tYou have harvested your field, and you are now ready to pick the yellow onion, as instructed by the Novice Farmhand. Make your way to a nearby workbench to pick through your crops.\n6\tThe recipe is complete. Do not eat or sell the yellow onion! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Farmhand.\t\n",
[7613]="700626AB\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Farmhand to learn more about farming and set yourself on a path to good eating.\t\n2\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to grow the yellow onion. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Farmers are normally purchased from vendors or discovered while farming. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, plant a yellow onion field on farmland\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a crop of yellow onions. First, however, you must plant your yellow onion field. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Farming tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: In order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Farming requires a farmland.\n4\tCollect the fair yellow onion crop\030Activate the Track Crops skill\tThe Novice Farmhand provided you with the ingredients necessary to grow yellow onions. You must now harvest your yellow onion field and obtain a fair yellow onion crop. To find the field, activate the Track Crops skill.\n5\tUsing the ingredients you have, pick a yellow onion at the workbench\tYou have harvested your field, and you are now ready to pick the yellow onion, as instructed by the Novice Farmhand. Make your way to a nearby workbench to pick through your crops.\n6\tThe recipe is complete. Do not cook or sell the yellow onion! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Farmhand.\t\n",
[7614]="70025AF2\n1\tYou should speak with the Supplier to learn more about forestry.\t\n2\tThe Supplier provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the forester recipes. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for foresters are found among fallen branches or from the many beasts lurking in the wild, and some are purchased from suppliers. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a piece of brushed light leather\030Using the ingredients you received, craft a thin rowan board\tThe Supplier provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a piece of brushed light leather and a thin rowan board.\n4\tThe recipes are complete. Do not sell the brushed light leather or thin rowan board! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Supplier.\t\n",
[7615]="700626AD\n1\tYou should speak with the Chief Supplier to learn more about forestry.\t\n2\tThe Chief Supplier provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the forester recipes. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for foresters are found among fallen branches or from the many beasts lurking in the wild, and some are purchased from suppliers. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a piece of brushed light leather at a workbench\030Using the ingredients you received, craft a thin rowan board at a workbench\tThe Chief Supplier provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a piece of brushed light leather and a thin rowan board. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Forester tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: In order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Forestry requires a workbench.\n4\tThe recipes are complete. Do not sell the brushed light leather or thin rowan board! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Supplier.\t\n",
[7616]="70025AF3\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Jeweller to learn more about jewelcrafting.\t\n2\tThe Novice Jeweller provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the copper ring recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Jewellers are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospector profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredient you received, craft a copper ring\tThe Novice Jeweller provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a copper ring. Approach the workbench and prepare the copper ring.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the copper ring! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Jeweller.\t\n",
})
